## I2 · Write Path (8 domains, highest risk — R12)

Wire every `toast.success()` stub to a real mutation. Key rules:
- No optimistic UI on ledger operations
- `Idempotency-Key` per user intent, not per HTTP attempt
- Validation errors on the right form fields, preserve user input
- 409 → "someone else changed this" + refresh, never silent overwrite
- Action endpoints, never `PATCH {status}`
- Bulk actions: partial-failure rendered row by row

## I3 · Acceptance

Evidence upload flow, localization sweep, 12 acceptance scenarios (§11), historical import rehearsal, UAT with real users, cutover plan.

## Sequencing Rule

I0 blocks I1/I2/I3. Each I1 domain swap blocks the same domain in I2. I2 blocks I3.
